Title: Nutts Corner: Man dies after single vehicle crash in County Antrim
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Police', 'Text': 'Police said the man was the driver of a white Volkswagen Golf which was involved in a single-vehicle incident in Ballyhill Road about 17:50 BST on Saturday.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 122}}, {'Speaker': 'Police', 'Text': 'Police added that a male passenger was taken to hospital with injuries, which are not believed to be life-threatening at this time.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 118}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'The ambulance service also attended but the driver died at the scene.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 65}}, {'Description': 'The Ballyhill Road was closed following the crash, but has now reopened.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 119, 'EndChar': 184}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'There is an old looking shed and wrought iron gate on the right of the picture. There is a lot of rubble at the entrance to the shed, which has a corrugated iron orange roof. There is a road on the left and some flowers have been tied to the gate. There are also some orange arrow markings on the ground in front of the shed.'}]}
